From d231a7c5bd1f10970d52ad1a134278394da0cc04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahmed Al-Nassif <mr.ahmed.nassif@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 22:59:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/24] f2fs: reduce timeout for uncongestion

On high fs utilization, congestion is hit quite frequently and waiting for a
whooping 20ms is too expensive, especially on critical paths.

Reduce it to an amount that is unlikely to affect UI rendering paths.

The new times are as follows:
  100 Hz  => 1 jiffy   (effective: 10 ms)
  250 Hz  => 2 jiffies (effective: 8 ms)
  300 Hz  => 2 jiffies (effective: 6 ms)
  1000 Hz => 6 jiffies (effective: 6 ms)

Co-authored-by: Danny Lin <danny@kdrag0n.dev>
Signed-off-by: Park Ju Hyung <qkrwngud825@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Ahmed Al-Nassif <mr.ahmed.nassif@gmail.com>
Rebased onto android13-5.15-lts: the generic patch's context no longer matches
here and it only applied with fuzz. Same added/removed lines.
---
diff --git a/fs/f2fs/f2fs.h b/fs/f2fs/f2fs.h
--- a/fs/f2fs/f2fs.h
+++ b/fs/f2fs/f2fs.h
@@ -579,8 +579,8 @@
 
 #define DEFAULT_RETRY_IO_COUNT	8	/* maximum retry read IO or flush count */
 
-/* congestion wait timeout value, default: 20ms */
-#define	DEFAULT_IO_TIMEOUT	(msecs_to_jiffies(20))
+/* congestion wait timeout value, default: 6ms */
+#define	DEFAULT_IO_TIMEOUT	(msecs_to_jiffies(6))
 
 /* maximum retry quota flush count */
 #define DEFAULT_RETRY_QUOTA_FLUSH_COUNT		8
